Accepted by chronium, 2026-10-24: the worker completion predicate is evaluated
under its existing task mutex. This corrects concurrent plain-state reads;
actual workers, priorities, queueing, pause and futures are retained. Remove
the local patch when the selected upstream revision contains the fix.

Optional feature macros remain caller-selected. Use the same configuration
before the first include in every translation unit of one consumer. Priority
and pause macros change the C++ class and its inline methods. No compiled
implementation or replacement scheduler is supplied.

Original Pyxis recipe and documentation use MPL-2.0. Their complete source and
the upstream-derived patch are installed under share/thread-pool/pyxis, with
both licenses recorded alongside this notice.
